<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>SC Mauritania Pt 1 - 2011</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;[An ode to the classic Origin/Chris Roberts game Strike Commander, which my poor 386 could never satisfactorily deliver but with which I was greatly enamored.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;I thought it would be fun to recreate some of its' missions in Command.&amp;nbsp; We start at the beginning...]&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The past twenty years has seen unprecedented world-wide upheaval with the uncivil fracturing of the Soviet Union, failed interventions in the Mid-East and continental environmental disasters.&amp;nbsp; Across the globe&amp;nbsp;old political orders fall, energy resources dwindle&amp;nbsp;and economies collapse.&amp;nbsp; Mercenaries become a commonplace tool as governments and powerful corporations vie among each other to protect or assert their interests.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Mauritania, July 2011&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Struggling with an externally-funded rebellion, the leadership of the North African nation of Mauritania has turned to employing&amp;nbsp;private military&amp;nbsp;forces to stem their losses.&amp;nbsp; The Turkish-based &lt;STRONG&gt;Wildcats&lt;/STRONG&gt;, a mercenary fighter squadron composed of F-16 fighters, has been retained and is beginning operations from a remote Strike Base in the Western Sahara.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
